d decision.scope (project|bundle; empty = project, which is the unchanged default). Membership is a table and not a column because a project can belong to several bundles (a harness is both an ecosystem member and its own project). Acceptance: `auger init` declares both tables idempotently; a bundle-scoped decision round-trips with its scope intact; the default for an existing decision row is project (no behaviour change on migration); a bundle_member naming a project with no scheduler row is REFUSED with a clear error.","review_notes":null,"status":"complete","title":"[P1] bundle model: bundle + bundle_member tables, and decision.scope (project|bundle) — SPEC-002 1","updated_at":"2026-09-21T08:09:00.714258+00:00","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"bundle + bundle_member tables and decision.scope per SPEC-002 section 1: closed sets (BUNDLE_STATUSES/BUNDLE_ROLES) refused by name like EDGE_KINDS; existence-checked writes mirroring edge()/facet(); membership verified READ-ONLY against the scheduler projects DB (candidate list: the row-named path first, then ~/.hermes/coding-hermes/scheduler.db, AUGER_SCHEDULER_DB exclusive override; a 0-byte file counts as absent, and the row-named path IS 0 bytes on this host) with a graceful 'cannot verify' refusal when no fleet DB is readable; default scope travels as an ABSENT key so pre-scope namespaces keep working, and a bundle scope on such a namespace is downgraded with an explicit WARNING, never silently. 10 new tests. Worker commit b92d32f.","detail":{"fingerprint":"bfb9977dd60d5efb991b9a0e041662f39cb6669df48cca4217019f03d3213bd3"}}
-{"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["bundle","engine","gate","spec-002"],"ci_result":null,"commit_hash":"4dfd98e","completed_at":"2026-09-21T10:19:00+00:00","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-20T23:39:09.391009+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":"2026-09-21T08:40:11+00:00","exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":null,"guard_result":"PASS","id":"AUG-010","lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P1","reasoning":"docs/SPEC-002-bundles.md sections 2.1 and 2.2. The two behaviours that make bundling worth having. (a) GATE searches EVERY member's namespace: evidence = recall_many([ns(m) for m in bundle_members(p)], q) - this is cross-project decision dedupe, so if terminal-jail already decided how a sandbox isolates the filesystem, bunker LINKS that answer instead of re-deciding it and drifting; the satisfies edge gains src_project so the reader sees it came from a sibling. (b) IMPACT crosses the boundary for bundle-scoped decisions only: a project-local decision never crosses (or every answer reaches every project and the pass is quadratic again), and a breaks edge INTO A SIBLING IS AN ESCALATION, NOT A SILENT CHANGE - the engine records the break and surfaces it, it never rewrites another project's spec. Depth triage for a bundle-scoped decision takes the MAX blast radius across members. Acceptance: a question already answered in a sibling namespace is LINKED not asked; a bundle-scoped answer that invalidates a sibling decision produces a breaks edge naming that sibling and an escalation row; a project-scoped answer produces NO cross-project edge.","review_notes":null,"status":"complete","title":"[P1] bundle-aware GATE and cross-boundary IMPACT — SPEC-002 2.1/2.2","updated_at":"2026-09-21T12:36:15+00:00","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"feat(bundles): bundle-aware gate + cross-boundary impact (SPEC-002 2.1/2.2). Gate pools recall across bundle-member namespaces and links cross-project answers with a satisfies edge carrying src_project; a bundle-scoped answer walks its siblings (bundle_impact): change -> affects edge, invalidate -> breaks edge + escalation row (recorded, never rewritten); project-scoped answers cross no boundary; no-membership gate unchanged; JEV unavailable = skip member, fail-closed. 10 new tests (55 total). Foreman gate re-run: GATE PASS (live smoke incl). Tier-2 verdict 6f07c47b COMPLETE/PASS. CI run on main: SUCCESS.","detail":{"fingerprint":"283676204b1d0d22ad891821c7718a6ff3e8b02e4b5f5898fca7f2931ec525e7"}}
-{"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["duckbrain","http","reliability"],"ci_result":"GREEN","commit_hash":"f2cb325","completed_at":"2026-09-21T05:29:15.925832+00:00","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-09-21T00:28:47.802316+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":["auger.py","tests/conftest.py","tests/test_auger.py"],"foreman_note":"Merged into main as a7a19a9 (merge of wt/AUG-011) by tick 3 (auger-2026-09-21-04-48-59); gate re-run on the merged tree: py_compile, ruff clean, pytest 35 passed (31+4 new), smoke 15/0, GATE PASS; pushed, parity 0. GitReins tier-1 PASS at work commit. Tier-2 COMPLETE same tick (verdict 3b564390, tier-1 PASS; folded into review_notes). Follow-up: row item (ii) DuckBrain-wide stale-registry class still needs a duckbrain board row.","guard_result":"PASS","id":"AUG-011","lines_added":218,"lines_removed":4,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P2","reasoning":"DuckBrain's HTTP API runs a token-bucket limiter (src/auth/ratelimit.ts; live limit measured at 600 requests/minute per IP, X-RateLimit-Limit: 600). auger hit it in two distinct ways during this tick: (a) the transport had no retry, so a 429 propagated to the caller and cmd_init then read the ERROR body as a namespace list and crashed ('str' object has no attribute 'get') while leaving its namespace behind; (b) a test namespace leaked because the teardown DELETE itself 429'd. (a) is fixed in auger (d2dcad3: bounded retry honouring retryAfter/Retry-After, plus init failing loudly on a non-200 list). (b) is NOT fixed: teardown_namespace does not retry, so a 429 during teardown still leaks a registry row. Separately, and this one is DuckBrain's, not auger's: DELETE /api/namespaces/<n> leaves NO record of a namespace whose directory is gone — 19 stale test entries accumulated in /api/namespaces (cleared by hand this tick) because the directory removal and the registry delete are independent. Scope: (i) auger teardown retries on 429; (ii) check whether the stale-registry class is DuckBrain-wide (it affects any tool that creates namespaces) and file it against the duckbrain board if so.","review_notes":"TIER-2 VERDICT FOLD (same tick): verdict 3b564390 (.gitreins/history/2026-09-21/3b564390/verdict.json, tracked in git), evaluated_at 2026-09-21T05:24:41.759754, tier-1 PASS, tier-2 COMPLETE. The judge evaluated at tip 67cc6d9 (after the AUG-013 commit); the graded merge content is a7a19a9 == work commit f2cb325. Async job job-a9f34c12fc4243e7a92552545282094f.","status":"complete","title":"[P2] DuckBrain's 429 backpressure is unhandled by every caller (found by AUG-006's tier-1 judge)","updated_at":"2026-09-21T05:29:15.925832+00:00","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"Worker commit f2cb325 in wave worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-011 (branch wt/AUG-011, dispatched by tick auger-2026-09-21-03-36-50). Premise corrected on the record: the teardown DELETE was already retried via the inline _req 429 path from d2dcad3; what was missing was a PIN. Landed: auger.delete_namespace(ns, retries=TEARDOWN_RETRIES=8) owns the deletion (404 = gone), auger.db(forwards retries), conftest tears down through the same helper (no-bypass asserted via counter relationship: 2 _req calls issuing 3 HTTP requests), 4 new offline cases (429-then-200 completes; Retry-After header honoured; 429 on registry re-check does not fail a successful teardown; permanently saturated limiter gives up BOUNDED and REPORTS the leak). RED control: retries=0 hole makes the leak case fail as claimed. Item (ii) of the row — whether the stale-registry class is DuckBrain-wide — remains OPEN and is DuckBrain's to decide; file it on the duckbrain board.","detail":{"fingerprint":"8425cea54036fc94fe95db80c6a9f9fa489280696324b922d867f823f350270c"},"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-011","branch":"wt/AUG-011"}
